# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, checking the repo out on Windows and touching files with an
# editor that writes CRLF rewrote every .tex/.cls/.md/licence in the tree,
# producing diffs of 8000+ changed lines with zero content change and leaving
# the working tree permanently dirty.
#
# text=auto: git stores text files with LF in the repo and converts to the
# platform's native ending on checkout. Binary files are auto-detected and
# left alone.
* text=auto

# Belt-and-braces for the binaries that live here, so they are never
# line-ending converted even if auto-detection is wrong.
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.eot    binary
*.zip    binary

# LaTeX sources are text but must keep LF in the repo.
*.tex    text
*.cls    text
*.sty    text
*.bib    text
